[1mNAME[0m
       sed - stream editor for filtering and transforming text

[1mSYNOPSIS[0m
       sed [-V] [--version] [--help] [-n] [--quiet] [--silent]
           [-l N] [--line-length=N] [-u] [--unbuffered]
           [-E] [-r] [--regexp-extended]
           [-e script] [--expression=script]
           [-f script-file] [--file=script-file]
           [script-if-no-other-script]
           [file...]

[1mDESCRIPTION[0m
       [4mSed[24m is a stream editor.  A stream editor is used to perform basic text transformations on an input stream (a file or input from a pipeline).  While in some ways similar to an ed‐
       itor  which  permits scripted edits (such as [4med[24m), [4msed[24m works by making only one pass over the input(s), and is consequently more efficient.  But it is [4msed[24m's ability to filter text
       in a pipeline which particularly distinguishes it from other types of editors.

